text:
I saw with my eyes as I turned round;
The whole earth was lying before me ;
And it seemed to me that its walls were white,--
Its towers like ivory pillars reared against heaven.

There were so many men, and women,
And children too!

But they were all different-
Some had their hair tied back with ribbons;
Others wore white hats or sunbonnets;

The little girls' dresses were blue and pretty;
And red skirts showed that some women had money;
A few wore gray gowns; and there was one man

With a brown coat on him, hatless as he walked;
All round them came an endless throng;

O ! how strange and beautiful ’tis thus
That we may know God’s ways within us !

When at his voice we hear His call;
